"\n"
"This module adds to ``stock_capture`` an option per operation type to\n"
"put each read or weighed quantity in a new package, e.g. one package per\n"
"weighing of a variable weight product. It works on transfers and, with\n"
"``mrp_capture``, on manufacturing orders for the product to manufacture\n"
"and its byproducts.\n"
"\n"
"The packages get the package type set on the operation type, and their\n"
"labels are printed as Odoo prints them on \"Put in Pack\", with the\n"
"operation type options to print the package label.\n"
"\n"
"A quantity captured with a destination package given by the user goes to\n"
"that package, and components consumed or goods written off never get\n"
"one.\n"
"\n"
".. IMPORTANT::\n"
"   This is an alpha version, the data model and design can change at any time without warning.\n"
"   Only for development or testing purpose, do not use in production.\n"
"   `More details on development status <https://odoo-community.org/page/development-status>`_\n"
"\n"
"**Table of contents**\n"
"\n"
".. contents::\n"
"   :local:\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"In the operation type, under *Packages*:\n"
"\n"
"- Tick *New Package per Capture*.\n"
"- Optionally choose the *Capture Package Type* of the new packages.\n"
"\n"
"To print the label of each new package, in the *Hardware* tab tick\n"
"*Package Label* under *Print on \"Put in Pack\"* and choose its format.\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"The screens that capture quantities get the label printing action of the\n"
"captured lines with ``stock.move.line._capture_package_label_action()``.\n"
"\n"
"Bug Tracker\n"
"===========\n"
"\n"
"Bugs are tracked on `GitHub Issues <https://github.com/OCA/stock-logistics-barcode/issues>`_.\n"
"In case of trouble, please check there if your issue has already been reported.\n"
"If you spotted it first, help us to smash it by providing a detailed and welcomed\n"
"`feedback <https://github.com/OCA/stock-logistics-barcode/issues/new?body=module:%20stock_capture_package%0Aversion:%2020.0%0A%0A**Steps%20to%20reproduce**%0A-%20...%0A%0A**Current%20behavior**%0A%0A**Expected%20behavior**>`_.\n"
"\n"
"Do not contact contributors directly about support or help with technical issues.\n"
"\n"
